#===============================================================================
# @TYPE:       esd-vg-ic
# @FUNCTIONAL: CAM-B3LYP
# @BASIS:      6-31G(d)
# @SOLVENT:    CPCM(Methanol)
# @ORCA:       6.1.0
# @CHARGE:     1
# @MULT:       1
# @VERIFIED:   PENDING
#===============================================================================
# ESD(IC) — Internal Conversion Rate via Excited State Dynamics
# Method: VG (Vertical Gradient, default) — S₁ Hessian ≈ S₀ Hessian
#
# KEY SYNTAX NOTES (ORCA 6.1):
#   - ESD(IC) on main input line triggers IC rate mode
#   - nacme true in %tddft enables nonadiabatic coupling matrix elements
#   - etf true uses electron translation factor (recommended)
#   - gshessian: S₀ Hessian from Opt+Freq
#   - eshessian: S₁ Hessian (use S₀ Hessian for VG approximation)
#   - usej true: Duschinsky rotation (recommended)
#
# DO NOT USE: do_ic (not a valid keyword), ic_method vg (not valid)
#===============================================================================

! CAM-B3LYP RIJCOSX 6-31G(d) CPCM(Methanol) ESD(IC) TightScf

%maxcore 3072

%pal
   nprocs 16
end

%tddft
  nroots 5
  iroot 1
  nacme true
  etf   true
  tda   true
end

%esd
  gshessian "<MOL>.hess"
  eshessian "<MOL>.hess"
  usej true
end

* xyz 1 1
  <INSERT S1 OPTIMIZED GEOMETRY HERE>
*